    <statement><p>Consider the following functions <m>f: \lbrace 1,2,3,4\rbrace \to \lbrace 1,2,3,4,5\rbrace</m>.  For each, determine whether it is (only) injective, (only) surjective, bijective, or neither injective nor surjective.</p>
<p><ol>
<li>
<p><m>f = \begin{pmatrix}1 \amp  2 \amp  3 \amp  4 \\ 2 \amp  2 \amp  1 \amp  4\end{pmatrix}</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>f = \begin{pmatrix}1 \amp  2 \amp  3 \amp  4 \\ 4 \amp  3 \amp  2 \amp  1\end{pmatrix}</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>f = \begin{pmatrix}1 \amp  2 \amp  3 \amp  4 \\ 2 \amp  3 \amp  4 \amp  5\end{pmatrix}</m></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
